# nazu is zero-conf: a fresh `docker compose up` works with NO .env file.
# Almost all configuration — features, GitHub tokens, OAuth, Cloudflare,
# local login, the Anthropic key — is set in the in-app Settings UI and
# persists in the database (the postgres volume), independent of where you
# launched compose from.
#
# This file is ONLY for infrastructure overrides and the few host-coupled
# values that can't live in the DB. Copy to .env if you need any of them.

# ── Infra connection overrides (defaults target the Compose services) ────
# DATABASE_URL=postgres://nazu:nazu@postgres:5432/nazu
# MINIO_ENDPOINT=http://minio:9000
# MINIO_ACCESS_KEY=minioadmin
# MINIO_SECRET_KEY=minioadmin
# MINIO_BUCKET=nazu-documents
# FALKORDB_ADDR=falkordb:6379
# FALKORDB_GRAPH=second_brain

# ── Compose / service control ───────────────────────────────────────────
# Pinned so the web app's in-container `docker compose` targets the same
# project/network as the host. Keep in sync with the host project name.
COMPOSE_PROJECT_NAME=nazu

# ── Caddy (tls profile) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# TLS certs are genuinely host files, so these stay in env. Required before
# enabling the tls service. NAZU_TLS_CERT/KEY are absolute host paths,
# bind-mounted into caddy at the same path.
# NAZU_HOSTNAME=your.host.example
# NAZU_TLS_CERT=/etc/ssl/nazu/your-host.pem
# NAZU_TLS_KEY=/etc/ssl/nazu/your-host-key.pem

# ── Local identity label (optional) ─────────────────────────────────────
# Email stamped on local / Basic-auth requests.
# NAZU_LOCAL_USER_EMAIL=local@nazu.local

# ── Agent / MCP access (optional) ───────────────────────────────────────
# Static API key(s) for non-interactive agents (the Memory MCP, scripts).
# Sent as `Authorization: Bearer <key>` or `X-API-Key`. Comma-separate to
# allow multiple clients. Leave unset to keep agent access off. Generate with
# `openssl rand -hex 32`. The same value goes in the @nazu/mcp client env.
# NAZU_API_KEY=
